{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "d4f21c80-1e42-4c8a-9f31-0ab1cd2e0200"/*AudioLevel*/,
  "Description": "A level-meter tap for the audio graph.\n\nPasses the wired audio sources through unchanged and outputs their combined level as a float for reactive control — e.g. driving a [DuckAudioLevel] or visuals.\n\nWire it inline (source → AudioLevel → [AudioBus]) for reliable metering of every source type, including timeline [AudioClip]s. A side branch (tapping a source without routing through to a bus) can only meter generator-type sources, not timeline clips. The level trails the audible signal by about a frame.\n\nLike every node in the audio graph, this is only heard once the chain reaches an [AudioBus] that is itself being evaluated — pinned to an output window, or wired into the render chain. A chain that ends nowhere is silent.",
  "InputUis": [
